@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title 17. Technology Options Comparison (Current Context)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "Option A\nSpring AI + LangGraph4J + Redis\n(Current/Recommended)" as A
rectangle "Option B\nSpring AI + custom loop\n(no graph engine)" as B
rectangle "Option C\nAlternative orchestration stack\n(additional framework)" as C

note bottom of A
- already implemented in current source
- CompiledGraph + Redis checkpoint/store in use
- MCP integration path is stable
- supports mixed transport (SSE + stdio) via MCP factory
- supports scoped controllers + unrestricted HttpChatController
- lowest migration risk
end note

note bottom of B
- possible for very simple flows
- state transitions become implicit in service code
- checkpoint/handoff logic harder to enforce
end note

note bottom of C
- possible future path
- larger framework surface and migration cost
- needs adapter rewrite for current ports
end note

A --> B : simpler architecture, weaker state guarantees
A --> C : lower migration effort from current code

@enduml
